[ ] Run the facilitator as root on the dev pod $Darrion, 2026-10-08: get the dev pod working and the assistant running there as root, working from there. The charter's next practical work: build and boot the dev profile and perform one root-agent task.$ !2 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-0ffc-7750-887c-9d8d6c3e6dc0
    >[ ] Build the dev-pod image and boot it in a disposable VM with root SSH $Stock path first: disposable signing keys from mkosi genkey in a private 0700 dir, scripts/mkosi-arch dev-pod build, boot with mkosi vm / systemd-vmspawn, root key via stock systemd credential ssh.authorized_keys.root. Check first why earlier candidates were built in a separate builder VM (Fedora SELinux relabeling, or desktop isolation?) and whether that still applies to Arch. Bounded resources, owned cleanup, keys removed afterwards.$ !2 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-100c-7431-805f-1e589a65ea81
    >[=] Decide how an agent authenticates on the dev pod $NEEDS DECISION: the pod holds no durable secrets and provider auth stays on the controller, but a harness running on the pod needs provider auth. Recommendation: a dedicated token (like agent-sandbox's claude_token from claude setup-token), passed at VM start as a systemd credential so it lives only in /run, never in the image or on disk, and gone on reboot or wipe. Alternative: the harness stays on the desktop and drives the pod over SSH, which keeps auth off the pod entirely but means I am not really running there.$ !2 +human ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-101a-751e-ae45-a70b3b660cc1
    >[ ] Add the agent harness to the dev-pod profile $Arch images have no agent CLI yet; add only what the task needs (claude, pi), following the image's existing package conventions.$ !3 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-1029-74fa-9963-11180d7f7709
    >[ ] Run one root-agent task on the dev pod and harvest it $The proof: the assistant works from the pod as root on a real task; changes come back to the desktop by harvest, since the pod cannot push.$ !3 ^2026-10-08T16:10 #01a11dc8-1038-74a7-a34a-fb724a968444
